\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The effect survives a change of state space, a change of generative objective, and a $5\times $ range of clutter. The rigid body is an L-shaped union of five spheres whose state is a full pose, chosen to have trivial symmetry so the domain is not secretly easier; both models are below their own floor at $20$ epochs and only the reduced one clears it. The density rows are freshly generated layouts at densities neither model was trained on. Single seed except the DDPM $20$-epoch row.}}{10}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:replications}{{4}{10}{The effect survives a change of state space, a change of generative objective, and a $5\times $ range of clutter. The rigid body is an L-shaped union of five spheres whose state is a full pose, chosen to have trivial symmetry so the domain is not secretly easier; both models are below their own floor at $20$ epochs and only the reduced one clears it. The density rows are freshly generated layouts at densities neither model was trained on. Single seed except the DDPM $20$-epoch row}{table.4}{}}
